diagnosis_text:
A complete four-layer diagnostic sweep of the ospf_enterprise_static topology found no fault. Phase 1 (ICMP reachability) showed zero packet loss across all tested host pairs. Phase A infrastructure sweep confirmed clean L2 identity (no duplicate MACs), no ACL/firewall drop rules, correct IP addressing on both hosts, and no resolver or gateway divergence. Phase B showed all six FRR/OSPF routers healthy — every daemon active, every neighbour in Full state, ten routes present on each router — with no tc traffic shaping anywhere. Phase D service_snapshot performed the precise test described in the ticket: it resolved `web0.local` from host_1_1_1_1 and issued an HTTP GET to that URL. DNS correctly returned 10.200.0.3 and the server replied HTTP 200 in 5 ms. web_server_0 also answered its own localhost HTTP probe with 200. The pressure sweep found no stress tools, no CPU pressure, and no socket spikes on any device. There is no mechanism (no flap script, no link-down history, no daemon restart entry) that could explain a past or intermittent fault. The helpdesk report cannot be confirmed from live evidence; the web portal and DNS server are both fully operational at the time of investigation.
=== END ===